sequenceDiagram
    participant kernel as linux kernel

    
    
    

    create participant initrd
    kernel->>initrd: unpack and launch
    initrd->>initrd: initialize hardware
    initrd->>initrd: check hash of wabbit-initrd
    create participant winit as wabbit-initrd
    initrd->>winit: launch
    winit->>+kernel: stop the world. freeze all other processes<br>by walking process tree and calling SIGSTOP
    kernel->>initrd: FREEZE BITCH
    initrd-->>kernel: [silence]
    kernel-->>-winit: done.
    winit->>+kernel: make /lib/modules and<br/>/sysroot/lib/modules immutable via bpf
    kernel-->>-winit: ack, confirm protections are in place
    winit->>+kernel: test write perms of /l/m
    kernel-->>-winit: EPERM
    winit->>+kernel: attach standalone tracepoint protections against<br/>kmod loading from outside /lib/modules
    kernel-->>-winit: protections attached, here's an fd
    winit->>+kernel: test loading a dummy module
    kernel-->>-winit: errno 0 but no action taken
    note over winit,kernel: this should ideally cause <br> module loading to fail silently.
    winit->>+kernel: make bpf maps for allowed bpf pids and<br> whether to allow making new map fds
    kernel-->>-winit: done, here are fds. no more fds will<br> be handed out
    winit->>+kernel: restrict bpf syscalls based on pid, temporarily
    kernel-->>-winit: ok, bpf can't be called by pids not in map
    winit->>+kernel: verify by spawning another process and<br> doing a bpf syscall
    kernel-->>-winit: not allowed!
    

    winit->>+kernel: pin everything to bpffs
    kernel-->>-winit: done
    winit->>+kernel: can i access this at the location i expect?
    kernel-->>-winit: yes
    winit->>+kernel: copy wabbit to<br>initrd
    kernel-->>-winit: copied
    winit->>+kernel: begin poll for /sysroot to be mounted
    kernel-->>+winit: will notify when sysroot is ready
    winit->>+kernel: resume the world
    kernel-->>-winit: done
    note over initrd: other shit happens
    note over kernel,initrd: sysroot gets mounted
    kernel->>-winit: notify of sysroot being mounted
    winit->>+kernel: stop the world
    kernel-->>-winit: ack, world stopped
    winit-->>+kernel: mount necessary runtime filesystems (cgroupfs...)
    kernel-->>-winit: mounted, here are fds
    winit->>+kernel: create wabbit cgroup
    kernel-->>-winit: done, here's fd
    winit->>+kernel: copy wabbit <br>to initrd
    kernel-->>-winit: done
    winit->>+kernel: start wabbit
    create participant wao as wabbit (outer)
    kernel->>-wao: start the initializer process with argv[0][0] set to @
    note over wao: to make sure wabbit-outer can see<br> into userspace later, it needs to<br> grab onto fses now before they<br> are moved to sysroot.
    wao->>+kernel: open file descriptors for /proc, /sys, /dev, etc
    kernel-->>-wao: here ya go
    wao-->>wao: keep those for later
    wao->>+kernel: read config from rootfs
    kernel-->>-wao: wspf data
    wao->>wao: verify config integrity
    wao->>+kernel: create maps based on configuration
    kernel-->>-wao: map creation successful
    wao->>+kernel: check accessibility and integrity of maps
    kernel-->>-wao: maps accessible

    wao->>+kernel: load and attach bpf protections in non-enforce mode
    create participant ebpf as wabbit-ebpf
    kernel->>+ebpf: attach to lsm and tracepoints
    ebpf-->>kernel: i am active but not enforcing.
    kernel-->>-wao: bpf programs attached. not enforcing.
    wao->>+ebpf: start self-tests
    loop self-test
        wao->>+kernel: do test action
        kernel->>+ebpf: can it do that?
        ebpf-->>-kernel: yes, but i'm logging it
        kernel-->>-wao: did action
    end
    ebpf-->>-wao: end self-tests
    wao->>+ebpf: did you catch all that?
    ebpf-->>-wao: yeah, here's a list
    wao->wao: self-tests done.
    wao->>ebpf: start enforcing.
    ebpf-->>wao: ENFORCING.
    loop self-test
        wao->>+kernel: do test action
        kernel->>+ebpf: can it do that?
        ebpf-->>-kernel: NO.
        kernel-->>-wao: [errno dependent on action]
    end
    wao->>winit: ready for you to back off.
    loop pre-shutdown self-test
        winit->>+kernel: do test action
        kernel->>+ebpf: can it do that?
        ebpf-->>-kernel: NO.
        kernel-->>-winit: [errno dependent on action]
    end
    note over winit: winit has done its job!
    winit-->>wao: i'm ready to die
    wao-->>winit: kys
    destroy winit
    winit->>kernel: exit


    



    create participant systemd
    initrd->>systemd: launch
    initrd->>systemd: switch root
    systemd->>systemd: do normal system startup
    wao->>+kernel: poll for the appearance of /run/systemd/private
    kernel-->>wao: will lyk
    note over wao: once systemd has started up, <br>notify wabbit
    

    wao->>+kernel: use the /proc fd, access "1/root" to see systemd's view of rootfs
    kernel-->>-wao: get the fd
    wao-->>+kernel: chroot into main root



    create actor red as red team
    red->red: bumble in
    note over red: red team is gonna<br>try to attack us.
    red->>kernel: i wanna load a kmod
    kernel-->>ebpf: check whether the red team's cgroup can load kmods
    ebpf-->>kernel: fuck no lmao what
    kernel-->>red: fuck all the way off

    note over blue: blue team sees logs,<br>wants to investigate
    blue->>wao: signed rpc: spawn /sysroot/bin/sh in rootfs<br>under the class "shell"
    wao->>wao: check signature,<br>resolve the class from the policy
    wao->>kernel: create ephemeral child cgroup<br>(run-<command id>) for the process
    kernel-->>wao: done!
    wao->>ebpf: grant this cgroup exactly<br>the class's permissions
    ebpf-->>wao: done!
    wao->>kernel: spawn process (it migrates itself<br>into its cgroup before exec)
    kernel-->>wao: done, here are its fds
    wao-->>blue: forward/attach fd to rpc caller binary to allow shell interaction
    blue-->>blue: you have a secured shell now!<br>(no class = deny-by-default)
    

    note over red: try to mess w/ cgroup
    red->>kernel: attempt to kill wabbit's cgroup
    kernel->>ebpf: check whether the red team's cgroup can touch wabbit's cgroup
    ebpf->>kernel: nuh uh :3
    kernel-->>red: HANDS OFF DA MOICHANDAISE

    note over red: try to edit ebpf map
    red->>kernel: use bpf() syscall
    kernel-->>ebpf: check whether the red team's cgroup can do that
    ebpf-->>kernel: what do you think
    kernel-->>red: respectfully, go shove a spear up your ass
    
    note over red: try to edit firewall rules
    red->>kernel: we would like to modify iptables configs
    kernel-->>ebpf: check whether the red team's cgroup can do that
    ebpf-->>kernel: no
    kernel-->>red: youw can't mawdify fiewwall wules, sowwy :/

    note over red: red finds a way in, <br> wabbit lets us take<br> it out quickly

    actor blue as blue team
    note over blue: blue team wins
    note over blue: blue gets a break from coding
    note over blue: and kisses a cute girl or smth

    